.TH PEEKIN-SETTINGS 1 2026-09-25 "PeekIn 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peekin-settings \- graphical settings for face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peekin-settings
.RB [ \-\-cli
.IR path ]
.br
.B peekin-settings \-\-dev \-\-config\-dir
.I dir
.B \-\-data\-dir
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
The PeekIn app, for the signed-in user.
It has three pages:
.TP
.B Settings
Where face login is used (sudo, login screen, lock screen, administrator
dialogs, text console), the camera, the scan time, the head-movement check,
the match threshold and the personal threshold, and messages.
.B System status
shows whether the configuration, camera, PAM integration and face models are
ready, and whether face login is paused after failed attempts, with a
.B Resume
button.
.TP
.B Face models
Add face models with a live camera preview, and remove them.
.TP
.B Test
Run the same recognition and head-movement check as a login, with live results.
.PP
The app runs unprivileged.
Reading and changing face models and settings goes through
.I /usr/libexec/peekin/peekin-helper
with
.BR pkexec (1),
so polkit asks for administrator authentication.
Settings are applied as one checked transaction; a change made elsewhere in
the meantime is detected and not overwritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cli " path"
The
.BR peekin (1)
binary to use (absolute path).
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Development mode: no pkexec, and private configuration and data directories
given with
.B \-\-config\-dir
and
.BR \-\-data\-dir .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peekin (1),
.BR peekin-config (5),
.BR pam_peekin (8)
